meta {
  name: Get latest analysis run for source
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/children/{{childId}}/analysis-runs/latest?sourceType=IepDocument&sourceId={{iepDocumentId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  sourceType: IepDocument
  sourceId: {{iepDocumentId}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # GET /api/children/{childId}/analysis-runs/latest

  NEW (unified-analysis refactor) — replaces `GET /api/ieps/{id}/analysis` and
  `GET /api/etrs/{id}/analysis`. The most recent run that included this document as a source, in the
  same shape `GetById` returns — see `GetById` for how `sections` is structured (ordinary sections,
  `iep_goals`, `etr_completeness`/`etr_eligibility`) — except `sections` here holds only the requested
  source's own sections, not every source's. Plus the two things a document page needs that a plain
  run read doesn't: the run's other sources, and whether the run is stale for *this* document.

  ## Query

  - `sourceType` (required) — `IepDocument | EtrDocument` for this page's two callers (the enum also
    has `ProgressReport`/`SharedDraftRevision`, but neither document page queries by those). Invalid
    value → `400`.
  - `sourceId` (required) — must belong to this child; an id from another child (or a document type
    that doesn't exist) resolves the same as "no run found" → `404`, never a cross-child leak.

  ## Responses

  - `200` — `data: AnalysisRunLatestDto`: every `AnalysisRunDto` field (see `GetById` for the full
    `sections` shape), except `sections` is filtered to only the sections belonging to the requested
    `sourceType`/`sourceId` (`sources` and `otherSources` still list every source in the run — only
    `sections` is narrowed). Plus two additions a document page needs that a plain run read doesn't:
    - `otherSources` — the run's sources other than the one matched, each `{ sourceType, sourceId, label }`,
      for a "part of a larger analysis, also covering …" note.
    - `stale` — `true` when the document has moved on since this run: it was reprocessed after the run
      started (document `updatedAt` later than the run's `createdAt`), or — IEP sources only — the
      run's `iep_goals` section for this source rates a `goalId` that is no longer among the document's
      current goals.
  - `400` — invalid `sourceType`.
  - `401` — missing/invalid bearer token.
  - `404` — child not found or no access to it, `sourceId` doesn't belong to this child, or no run
    includes this document yet ("No analysis found for this document."). This endpoint always returns
    `404` on failure (unlike `Create`/`GetByChild`, it never maps to `400`/`402`/`403`).

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": null,
    "data": {
      "id": 101,
      "childProfileId": 1,
      "status": "Completed",
      "overallSummary": "Both documents show consistent reading goals with gaps in progress data.",
      "crossDocSynthesis": {
        "summary": "The ETR's evaluation data aligns with the IEP's present levels.",
        "timeline": ["ETR completed 2026-03-15", "IEP finalized 2026-05-01"],
        "contradictions": [],
        "progression": "Reading fluency improved since the ETR baseline."
      },
      "overallRedFlags": [],
      "advocacyGapAnalysis": null,
      "parentGoalsSnapshot": [
        { "id": 5, "goalText": "Read at grade level by end of year", "category": "Academic", "displayOrder": 0 }
      ],
      "sources": [
        { "id": 201, "sourceType": "IepDocument", "sourceId": 35, "sourceLabel": "IEP dated 2026-05-01", "status": "Completed", "errorMessage": null },
        { "id": 202, "sourceType": "EtrDocument", "sourceId": 9, "sourceLabel": "ETR dated 2026-03-15", "status": "Completed", "errorMessage": null }
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": 301,
          "analysisRunSourceId": 201,
          "sectionKind": "iep_goals",
          "analysis": null,
          "goalAnalyses": [
            {
              "goalId": 77,
              "goalText": "Student will read 80 WPM with 90% accuracy",
              "domain": "Reading",
              "smartAnalysis": {
